# Relative tolerance on chi-squared for this project, overriding the suite's
# default of 1e-3.
#
# The hybrid model integrates the radial wave functions outward through the
# nuclear potential by Numerov -- some 545 steps of dr = 0.0275 fm out to the
# 15 fm matching radius -- and then matches to the Coulomb functions. That
# accumulates far more floating-point sensitivity than the plain Coulomb path,
# which libm computes in one go: the same compiler on the same machine, built
# -O0 instead of -O3, moves this project's segment 2 by 1.1e-3 and its total by
# 6.9e-4, while 13N and 13N_capture_ay move by 3e-6 under the same comparison.
#
# 1e-3 therefore pins nothing but the toolchain that recorded the reference,
# which is how this test failed on all three CI platforms while passing on the
# machine it was written on.
#
# 2e-2 is kept as a bound on toolchain noise, which is what it measures.
#
# It is NO LONGER calibrated against the per-pair failure mode, and the note
# that used to stand here was wrong about how much this chi-squared can see:
#
#     correct (pair 1 overrides the default with V0 = 20)   2.46215e6
#     the per-pair override ignored, default V0 = 40 used   2.46168e6   -0.02%
#
# The +12.7% separation recorded previously was an artefact of an unconverged
# target integral, not a physical sensitivity. Measured 2026-09-11 by refining
# the integration grid with both the current code and the code as it stood
# before the resonance-width estimator was fixed:
#
#     lattice pitch (points per width)      50        200       800
#     current code,  V0 = 20            2.46215e6  2.47531e6  2.47621e6
#     current code,  V0 = 40            2.46168e6  2.47484e6  2.47574e6
#     pre-fix code,  V0 = 20            2.46094e6  2.47431e6  2.47614e6
#     pre-fix code,  V0 = 40            2.44869e6  2.47379e6  2.47566e6
#     separation, pre-fix code            -0.50%     -0.02%     -0.02%
#
# Both codes converge to the same answer (2.4762e6, agreeing to 0.003%) and to
# the same -0.02% separation: the potential moves this project's chi-squared by
# a fifth of a percent at most, and the old large separation came from the grid
# responding to the potential through the penetrability in its width estimate,
# not from the cross section.
#
# So the per-pair SEMANTICS are covered by check_per_pair.py, which compares the
# configurations directly, and not by this bound. What the bound still catches is
# a gross change in the target-integration or Coulomb path.
#
# Note also that the reference is recorded at the project's shipped grid settings
# (10 sub-points, 20 widths, 50 points per width), which sit 0.6% below the
# pitch-converged 2.4762e6. That is deliberate -- the reference pins what the
# suite actually runs -- but raise points-per-width if you ever want this project
# to represent a converged integral.
2e-2
